# .graphifyignore — excludes for the codebase knowledge graph.
#
# WHY: the first build took the whole tree and produced 308,550 nodes, because
# ~55% of the files are tests (15,940 of 28,904). A query for
# "how does the SSE feed reach the chat panel" then matched
# `tests/qubit_cli/test_proxy.py` and `*.test.ts` files first — the graph was
# describing the test corpus, not the product. Upstream's own guidance:
# "Skip src/test. Test classes don't describe what production code does —
# they echo relationships already captured in src/main. Including them bloats
# node count 3-4x and degrades Leiden clustering quality."
#
# Keep infrastructure/config (it shows how services wire together), drop tests.

# --- tests (the big one: ~55% of files) ---
tests/
qubit_runtime/tests/
test/
__tests__/
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.test.js
*.test.mjs
test_*.py
*_test.py
conftest.py

# --- vendored / generated trees that are not our code ---
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
.graft/
sandbox/
_private_backup/
frontend/qubit-dist/
graphify-out/

# --- caches and artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

